+# Paused full-options NAP profile (2026-10-19)
+
+## Run
+
+Release client `19edc4a-git (20261019)` on OpenGL 4.6 / Mesa 23.2.1 and Intel HD Graphics 4600, 1280×720, VSync off. `--new-game --invulnerable=on` entered M01A in FP7. The renderer options and their exact startup arguments are recorded in [`launch-options.txt`](launch-options.txt); the first CSV row snapshots all 43 settings. Every renderer feature toggle is on, including shadows; VSync is off intentionally for profiling.
+
+The run used the 13-package active NAP manifest in [`active.json`](active.json). Every package archive was verified with `nexus-pack verify`; each archive's size and SHA-256 matched the manifest. Inputs were copied from `Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/profile-csv-20261019/`. The isolated application tree had no loose `DATA`, `data`, or `lib/data` directory. The runtime excerpt confirms data and interface loading, entry into `FP7_system`, and a 300-frame export without an INI file-not-found error.
+
+F1 paused the single-player scene; the last mission trigger was logged at 17:03:26. F9 started capture at 17:03:45, after the camera settled. No further mission triggers were logged during capture. `--invulnerable=on` applied only to the local embedded single-player player.
+
+## Result
+
+| Metric | p50 | p95 |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| FPS | 40.59 | 64.77 |
+| Frame interval | 24.64 ms | 29.63 ms |
+| Update + draw work | 8.59 ms | 14.89 ms |
+| GPU opaque pass | 5.49 ms | — |
+| GPU transparent pass | 1.21 ms | — |
+| GPU SSAO pass | 1.08 ms | — |
+| GPU shadow map | 0.20 ms | — |
+
+All 300 frames had GPU samples, with the maximum sample age at two frames. The cumulative dropped-simulation-tick counter rose from 1606 to 1866 across the capture. The mission trigger timeline stayed paused, but this counter still advances in the render/update loop; treat the capture as a paused-scene diagnostic, not a proof that every client-side clock or effect animation is frozen.
+
+This is one diagnostic profile on the old Intel/Mesa setup, not a stable FPS baseline, an A/B attribution, or an RTX 5060 performance forecast. Compare it only against a repeat with identical scene, pause-menu state, resolution, driver, and options.
